# Nothing here is needed to build, run, or publish the app.
#
# `pnpm install`, `pnpm dev` and `pnpm build:win` all work without a .env; the
# application creates and migrates its own database under Electron's userData.
# This file previously carried DATABASE_URL for Prisma, which the app no longer
# uses at all.
#
# It also previously carried GH_TOKEN, because publishing went through
# electron-builder. Releases are now uploaded by `pnpm release:win`, which uses
# the GitHub CLI's own credentials (`gh auth login`) - so no token is stored in
# the repo at all. See docs/releasing.md.
#
# The file is kept only so that this explanation has somewhere to live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cross-device sync (optional). Without these the feature is simply off.
#
# A "Desktop app" OAuth client from Google Cloud Console, with the consent
# screen scopes openid, email, profile and
# https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.appdata. Read at BUILD time (electron-vite
# exposes MAIN_VITE_* to the main bundle) and baked into the build; do not commit a
# real .env.
#
#   MAIN_VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
#   MAIN_VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
#
# For `pnpm dev`, which is unpackaged and so has no client by default, set the
# same two at run time instead:
#
#   SVWB_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / SVWB_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
#
# or point at the local fake Google (`node tools/sync-dev.mjs`):
#
#   SVWB_GOOGLE_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8788
